┌ Chats ───────────┐┌ Book club ───────────────────────────┐┌ People 2 of 3 ✓ ─┐
│#┌ Commands ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│@│                      messages (admins)                                   │ │
│#│/settings topic       admins or anyone: who can set the topic (admins)    │ │
│ │/status               see the server, connection, this room and the app   │ │
│ │/switch [room]        open a room; Tab or Up/Down completes the name      │ │
│ │/theme [name]         see or change the colors: phosphor or classic       │ │
│ │/title <name>         rename this room for everyone (admins)              │ │
│ │/topic [text]         see or set the topic; /topic --clear removes it     │ │
│ │/unmute               show this room's new-message count again            │ │
│ │/updates [on|off]     turn the daily check for a new version on or off    │ │
│ │/verify <name>        compare safety numbers with someone                 │ │
│ │/ then Enter          open this list to pick a command                    │ │
│ │/s then Up/Down       step through the commands that start with /s        │ │
│ │Tab or Up/Down        step through the rooms or names that fit after      │ │
│ │                      /switch, /invite or /join                           │ │
│ │Up/Down               bring back your earlier lines in this room          │ │
│ │Ctrl-C Ctrl-C         quit; one Ctrl-C copies the text you selected       │ │
│ │                                                                          │ │
└─│Drag over messages or the text in a box to copy it. To select with your   │─┘
┌─│terminal instead, hold Shift as you drag (Option or Fn on a Mac), or type │─┐
│ │/mouse off.                                                               │s│
└─└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[ Close ]─┘─┘
Up/Down pick a command · Enter use it · Esc close               socketchat 0.6.1
